-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  exe_build_errors.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: a link error mapped back

  An external routine no library defines fails at the link (ZB0016, the
  linker's own words), reported at the .pcpp line that calls it (the
  linker's referenced-by note, mapped like clang's locations).

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\exe_build_errors.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\exe_build_errors.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe exe_build_errors;

routine clink exe_missing_symbol(): int32; external;

begin
  println("{}", exe_missing_symbol()); // ERROR ZB0016: exe_missing_symbol
end.
